---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
import CaseSection from "../../components/CaseSection.astro";
import * as stylex from "@stylexjs/stylex";
import { caseStudyStyles } from "../../styles/caseStudyStyles";
import { portfolioStyles } from "../../styles/portfolioStyles";
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="AWS Fargate and Vault Infrastructure | Warre Snaet"
  description="Terraform for private ECS Fargate workloads on AWS: an ALB in front, Vault login through IAM, CloudWatch, autoscaling, and tested safeguards around deploys."
  kicker="Individual cloud infrastructure project, 2026"
  heading="AWS Fargate infrastructure with Vault workload identity"
  lead="Terraform for running private Fargate workloads, written with production in mind. The task definition contains no cloud credentials and no Vault tokens."
  meta={[
    { label: "Role", value: "Architecture, Terraform implementation, security model, tests, and documentation" },
    { label: "Stack", value: "AWS, Terraform, ECS Fargate, VPC, ALB, IAM, Vault, CloudWatch" },
    { label: "Scope", value: "Validated locally; not presented as a live AWS environment" },
  ]}
>
  <CaseSection label="Problem" title="An identity instead of a static secret">
    <p {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.paragraph)}>A small service had to be reachable from the internet while its containers stayed private. It also had to read its runtime content from Vault, without a long-lived Vault token or AWS access key sitting in the task definition.</p>
    <ul {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.list, caseStudyStyles.factsList)}>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>2 availability zones</strong>Public subnets for the load balancer and private subnets for Fargate.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>0 static tokens</strong>The ECS task role logs in to Vault directly through the AWS auth method.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>3 tested variants</strong>Plans for AWS only, with Vault, and with HTTPS through ACM.</li>
    </ul>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Architecture" title="Public load balancer, private tasks">
    <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.architecture)} role="img" aria-label="AWS architecture with internet traffic entering an Application Load Balancer, private Fargate tasks, IAM workload identity, Vault, and CloudWatch">
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowRow)}>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Ingress</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Application Load Balancer</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Public HTTP or ACM TLS across two availability zones</span></div>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Network</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Public subnets</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Internet gateway, the ALB, and a single NAT gateway to keep costs down</span></div>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Boundary</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Security groups</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Only the ALB can reach the tasks on port 8080</span></div>
      </div>
      <p {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowArrow)}>↓ private routing, no public task IPs ↓</p>
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowRow)}>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Compute</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>ECS Fargate service</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>App and Vault Agent containers with read-only root filesystems</span></div>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Identity</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>IAM task role</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Rotating credentials that sign the Vault login request</span></div>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Runtime data</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Ephemeral volume</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Vault Agent renders the one KV path the app is allowed to read</span></div>
      </div>
      <p {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowArrow)}>↓ operations and external secret service ↓</p>
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowRow)}>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Secrets</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Vault AWS auth</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Role bound to one exact ARN, short token lifetime, and a narrow read policy</span></div>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Observability</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>CloudWatch</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Container logs, 30-day retention, and Container Insights</span></div>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Reliability</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Health and scaling</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>ALB checks, container checks, rollback, and CPU autoscaling</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Runtime flow" title="Log in and fetch secrets before taking traffic">
    <ol {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.list)}>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>ECS gives the Vault Agent sidecar rotating task-role credentials.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>The agent signs an AWS IAM request and logs in to a Vault role that is bound to that exact task-role ARN.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>A least-privilege policy only allows reads from the one KV v2 path the app needs.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>The agent writes what it gets back to an ephemeral volume scoped to the task.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Once that file exists, the app reports healthy and the ALB starts sending it requests.</li>
    </ol>
    <p {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.paragraph)}>The app container itself never holds a Vault token or an AWS access key, and it has no permission to read any other secrets.</p>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Delivery" title="CI that can't deploy by accident">
    <p {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.paragraph)}>GitHub Actions checks the Terraform formatting, runs init without a backend, validates the configuration, and runs plan tests against mocked AWS and Vault providers, so it needs no credentials. On purpose, the workflow only has read access to the repository and has no cloud credentials at all.</p>
    <ul {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.list)}>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>The Makefile saves a Terraform plan and never applies anything while planning.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Applying needs a plan that already exists and has been reviewed, plus an explicit <code>ALLOW_APPLY=yes</code>.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>The service has a deployment circuit breaker that rolls back automatically.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>When ACM is configured, HTTP redirects to HTTPS with a modern TLS policy.</li>
    </ul>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Engineering" title="Reliability, security, and cost">
    <ul {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.list, caseStudyStyles.factsList)}>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Network isolation</strong>Only the load balancer is public. The tasks run privately and have no public IP addresses.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Workload identity</strong>Credentials managed by ECS take the place of long-lived keys and static Vault tokens.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Observability</strong>Both containers send structured output through awslogs, and Container Insights is enabled.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Availability</strong>The service runs in two availability zones with health checks, rolling replacement, rollback, and autoscaling.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Cost</strong>Most of the scheduling weight goes to Fargate Spot, scaling has fixed limits, and the NAT setup is a deliberate tradeoff for a demo.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Scope</strong>I verified the configuration and the three mocked plan variants locally. I don't present this as production experience with a live AWS deployment.</li>
    </ul>
    <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.links)}>
      <a {...stylex.attrs(portfolioStyles.link, caseStudyStyles.importantLink)} href="https://github.com/SnaetWarre/aws-fargate-vault-terraform">View repository and diagrams ↗</a>
    </div>
  </CaseSection>
</CaseStudyLayout>
